WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.189 --> 00:00:04.890
You want me to restate the question?

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:09.349
Well, the question is, "What is the political
establishment doing in the run up to Super

00:00:09.349 --> 00:00:10.349
Tuesday?"

00:00:10.349 --> 00:00:14.530
I think the obvious answer is praying.

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:18.090
One of the things that has been highlighted
by this election season, and particularly

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:22.440
the success of Donald Trump, is how weak the
establishment is.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:23.490
How you seen that?

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.970
On the Democratic side as well.

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:27.510
Bernie Sanders isn't even a Democrat.

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:33.430
Donald Trump, by a lot of measures, is a more
loyal Democrat than Bernie Sanders is.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:38.510
So there's that burning, yearning desire to
find a candidate that the "establishment"

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:42.019
can rally around as an alternative to Donald
Trump.

00:00:42.019 --> 00:00:46.750
And the fighting that we've been seeing on
the Republican side, where bizarrely for most

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:52.320
of this primary season the establishment candidates
have all been attacking each other rather

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:57.699
than attacking Donald Trump, that will sort
of no longer be tenable, but coming into Super

00:00:57.699 --> 00:01:03.079
Tuesday, everyone's pitch is gonna be, "I'm
the guy who can take down Trump," and who

00:01:03.079 --> 00:01:04.890
that guy is I have no clue whatsoever.

